<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICA MONEY MKT SHORTAGE FALLS TO 9.44 BLN RAND.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICA MONEY MKT SHORTAGE FALLS TO 9.44 BLN RAND.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage fell to 9.444 billion rand on Wednesday from 9.686 billion rand on Tuesday, the Reserve Bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates were steady at between 17.35 and 17.65 percent while the 90-day BA rate was also unchanged at between 16.65 and 16.95 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
